# A merge that leaves two formals unbound, the only callable result of the
# unit. add3 takes y, x and z; w holds merge(y: 5; add3), whose header is
# (int: x; int: z): 5 + 1 * 10 + 2 * 100. Entry 7.
fn: add3 (int: y; int: x; int: z) int
    return: y + x * 10 + z * 100

fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x; int: z) int
    return: merge(y: k; add3)

w: wrap 5
int: a (w: 1 2)
int: ok 7
if: a != 215
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
